00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:46.280
Already, Already, Already! Yet, Yet, Yet! Just, Just, Just! Ever, Ever, Ever!

38
00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:54.764
Never, Never, Never! Since, Since, Since! For years, For years! Recently, Recently, Recently!

39
00:01:55.064 --> 00:01:57.798
Clap, clap! Great chanting!

40
00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:17.267
Dara is getting ready for her trip. Has she packed her bag yet? Yes, she has already packed it. She has just bought her ticket. Has she ever been to Bangkok? No, never! She has wanted to go there for years. Recently, she has been saving money. She has studied English since she was ten.

41
